---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { href, person } from '../../lib/site';
const formKey = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_WEB3FORMS_KEY ?? '';
---

<Base title="Privacy" path="/privacy/" description="Exactly what this site collects: no cookies, no analytics, and what happens to a contact form.">
  <div class="wrap narrow">
    <header class="page-head">
      <p class="label">Privacy</p>
      <h1>What this site collects</h1>
      <p>Short version: almost nothing, and nothing that follows you around.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="prose body">
      <h2>No cookies, no analytics</h2>
      <p>This site sets no cookies and runs no analytics or tracking scripts. Fonts and every other file are served from this site, so your browser makes no requests to third parties while you read it.</p>
      <p>The numbers in the footer (load time, page weight, cookie count) are measured in your browser, shown to you, and sent nowhere.</p>

      <h2>Stored on your device</h2>
      <p>If you switch between light and dark themes, your choice is saved in your browser’s local storage under the key <code>theme</code>. It never leaves your device. Clearing site data removes it.</p>

      <h2>Contact form</h2>
      {formKey
        ? <p>When you send the contact form, the fields you filled in go to <a href="https://web3forms.com/privacy">Web3Forms</a>, which emails them to me. I use them only to reply to you, and I do not add you to any list.</p>
        : <p>The contact form does not send anything by itself: it opens your own email app with the message written, and you decide whether to send it.</p>}

      <h2>Hosting</h2>
      <p>The site is hosted on GitHub Pages. GitHub may log technical data such as IP addresses to keep the service running; see the <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub privacy statement</a>. I do not receive those logs.</p>

      <h2>Questions</h2>
      <p>Email <a href={`mailto:${person.email}`}>{person.email}</a>. If anything on this page changes, it will say so here first. <a href={href('/')}>Back home</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .narrow { max-width: 760px; }
  .body { margin: 24px 0 72px; }
  .body code { font: 0.9em var(--mono); background: var(--bg-raised); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 4px; padding: 1px 5px; color: var(--ink); }
</style>
